// Copyright (c) 2023-2024 Amazon.com, Inc.  All rights reserved.

(module ion_semantic_model "/fusion"
  '''
A denotational semantic model of Ion.

TODO
----
Terminology/Readability:
* The names around "document symbols" don't read well in prose. "local symbols"
  might be better but that requires careful editing to keep "local" precise.
* Figure out the proper name for `I`.  N? Z?
* Less type-switching via E[[]] denotations
  * Easier with distinct typed nulls
    * [LITERALS] Requires literals to render them as typewriter `null.foo`.
* Separate syntactic IVM from semantic spec-version?
* Print the Appendix in manually-assembled sections.
  * Should have a way to detect when a domain element is forgotten.
* Improve clarity around "Environment", "ModuleMap", "MacroEnv", and other lookups.

Major Components:
* [SHARED-MOD] Shared modules
  * [LOAD-MACRO] Load macros from shared modules
* [TUNNEL-MOD] Shared modules "tunneled" in shared symtabs
* [STRUCT-EE] Eexpr in field-position (struct inlining)

Features:
* [TL-MACRO] Support macro-shaped arguments in TL invocations.
* [PARAM-VALID] Do expand-time parameter validation in the macro or Transform
  * This is currently done in several places invocation-side, but makes more
    sense to happen once, macro-side.
  * Perhaps annoying for system macros.
  * User-macro Transform is created by `interp_xform`.
* [PARAM-TYPE] Declare and validate parameter types
* [DUPE-NAME] Reject duplicate names in parameter lists and `for` bindings.
* [LOAD-MAXID]`load` clause with max-id.
  * Unclear how to wire the exact/inexact match and max-id to later clauses.
    * Perhaps add LoadedModule to track that data, and return from ModuleMap.
  * Accept non-exact-match modules in `symbol_table`.
* Accept symbols in `symbol_table` inner lists: (symbol_table [sym1, "sym2"])
  * What about $0 ?
* [LOAD-MAXID] Module-level symtabs don't handle non-exact-match modules.
* [UNIFY-MACREF] Unify the two macro-resolution approachs (Eexp vs TL).
  * Probably migrate Eexp resolve_MacroRef functions to MacroEnv approach.
* [MAC-ID] Macro identity and proper ambiguity detection.
  * Also useful for any error reporting regarding the Macro, which is currently
    anonymous.
* [EXPORT-MOD] A module's macro_table can have a module name, as in EDs.
  * Matt had some confusion about this, points out that the module-name is not
    exported here, as it is for the ED variant.
* [EXPORT-REF] Export by macro reference.
* [EXPORT-FROM]
* [ED-USE] `use` clauses at directive-level; more wiring challenges.
  * Perhaps easier after [UNIFY-MACREF]?
* [VALID-NAME] Validate module, macro, and parameter names.
* [OPT-NAME] Optional macro names; can streamline some tests
* [VALID-FORM] Many forms need better validation of arity and argument type.
* [ERRMSG] Some 1.1 code relies on implicit type checking to reject erroneous
  forms, leading to unhelpful error messages.
* Implement Decimal, Float, Timestamp, Blob/Clob
* [ALIAS] Macro aliases; main impact is inability to import/rename/export macros.
* [USE-LOAD] Nested (use (load ...)) combination.
* [IMPORT] `import` clauses for both directive and module body


Defects:
* Spec says various encoding-directive elements are unannotated, but the
  model doesn't enforce that.
* SIDs and Macro addresses should be non-negative.
* The spec doesn't say that SST must have its annotation as the first one.
* [SST Semantics] "When mapping from string to symbol ID, there may be multiple
  associated IDs (the same string could appear twice as children of the symbols
  field). Implementations MUST select the lowest known ID, and all other
  associated IDs MUST be handled as if undefined."
  * Not sure what "handled as undefined" implies.
* Catalog construction should reject duplicate keys, so we don't imply anything
  about selection criteria.
* Struct denotations should be order-agnostic. See L.I.S.P. §5.5


Spec Issues: 1.1
----------------
* Rename "unqualified macro references" to "local"?  The latter is more precise
  though perhaps confusing in the E-expression case.
* Spec should ban the name $ion in load and import.
* Perhaps TL should treat all nulls as literals.  Easy and intuitive.
  * See quasi-literal explanations (§9.1.3)
  * null.symbol is the main thing that could be confusing.
* Spec says `symbol_table` rejects duplicate module names, and `$ion`.
  * I'm not sure the duplicate filter achieves anything; the same module can
    still appear under different names, with no difference in outcome.
* Spec doesn't describe how ungrouped tagless ZERO_OR_ONE is invoked without a
  value in either Text Eexps or TDL.
* Consider replacing `(retain *)` with just `(retain)`.  It eliminates some
  failure modes and reads nicely.  However, it may be surprisingly inconsistent
  compared to the non-empty behavior.
* Rationalize whether $ion can be in a `macro_table`.
  * Perhaps not a problem in $ion_encoding/macro_table since its version is
    implied.
  * If exported in-full from a shared module, it must be tied to that module's
    spec-version.  Which means diff exports can use diff system-module versions.


Spec Issues: 1.0
----------------
* No mention of possible annotations on imports field or its entries.
* "A version marker can also occur at non-initial positions at the top level,
  and it will have the same effect; when encountered below top-level, it has no
  processing effect and is treated as an ordinary user value."
  * Wrong, IVMs are syntactically distinct and cannot appear elsewhere.
* "Null elements declare undefined symbol IDs (“gaps”) within the sequence;
  implementations must handle requests for such symbols the same as if the
  requested ID beyond the end of the list."
  * BUT: "beyond the end" is an error.
  * AND: what does "requests for such symbols" mean?
* Content under "Imports" should use present/absent instead of defined/undefined
  since the latter has other meaning.
* [Symbol Zero] "$0 is only semantically equivalent to itself and to
  locally-declared SIDs with unknown text."
  * Probably better to treat the local case as something other than "unknown"
    so that term only applies to the SST case.  A local null entry is _known_ to
    be $0, but we know _nothing_ about an absent (or undersized substitute) SST.
  '''


  (require "/fusioncontrib/denotation/dsl")

  (provide (all_defined_out))


  (define_model Ion
    (import B I Unicode)
    (dom 'Unicode?*' = (** 'Unicode?'))


    //=============================
    // Application-layer Data Types

    (dom Value     = (* 'SymTok*'::annots Content::content))
    (dom 'Value**' = (** 'Value*'))

    (dom Content   = (+ Symbol List Sexp Struct NullNull Bool Int String
                        /*Decimal Float Timestamp Blob Clob*/))


    // Simple values require no expansion.
    // Their 'syntax' and 'application' denotations are the same.

    (dom DotNull  = (= DOTNULL) "Sentinel for typed nulls")
    (dom NullNull = (+ DotNull))
    (dom Bool     = (+ B DotNull))
    (dom Int      = (+ I DotNull))
    (dom String   = (+ Unicode DotNull))


    // Symbols

    (dom Sym0      = (= SYM0)            "The undefined symbol $0")
    (dom AbsentSym = (* Unicode::module I::index))
    (dom SymTok    = (+ Unicode Sym0 AbsentSym))
    (dom Symbol    = (+ SymTok DotNull))


    (fn SymTok_matches ((s SymTok) (u Unicode) -> B)
      (and (element_of s Unicode)
           (= (lower s Unicode) u)))

    (fn Symbol_matches ((s Symbol) (u Unicode) -> B)
      (and (element_of s SymTok)
           (SymTok_matches (lower s SymTok) u)))

    (fn Value_is_symbol_matching ((v Value) (u Unicode) -> B)
      (and (element_of (Value_content v) Symbol)
           (Symbol_matches (lower (Value_content v) Symbol) u)))

    (fn 'Value?_is_symbol_matching' ((v 'Value?') (u Unicode) -> B)
      (and (opt_is_present v) (Value_is_symbol_matching (opt_value v) u)))

    (fn Value_strtext ((v Value) -> Unicode)  (lower (Value_content v) String Unicode))

    (fn Value_symtext ((v Value) -> Unicode)
      (if (element_of (Value_content v) Symbol)
        (lower (Value_content v) Symbol SymTok Unicode)
        (wrong "Expected a symbol: " v)))

    (fn Value_int     ((v Value) -> I      )  (lower (Value_content v) Int I))


    // Containers

    (dom List     = (+ 'Value*' DotNull))
    (dom Sexp     = (+ 'Value*' DotNull))
    (dom Struct   = (+ 'Field*' DotNull))
    (dom Field    = (* SymTok::name Value::value))


    (fn Value_listElements ((v Value) -> 'Value*')
      (lower (Value_content v) List 'Value*'))

    (fn Value_seqElements ((v Value) -> 'Value*')
      (if (element_of (Value_content v) Sexp)
        (lower (Value_content v) Sexp 'Value*')
        (lower (Value_content v) List 'Value*')))


    (fn Fields_get ((fs 'Field*') (u Unicode) -> 'Value*')
      (if (seq_is_empty fs)
        (seq 'Value*')
        (let [(f (seq_head fs)),
              (vs (Fields_get (seq_tail fs) u))]
          (if (SymTok_matches (Field_name f) u)
            (seq_prepend (Field_value f) vs)
            vs))))

    (fn Struct_get ((s Struct) (u Unicode) -> 'Value*')
      (Fields_get (lower s 'Field*') u))

    (fn Struct_get1 ((s Struct) (u Unicode) -> 'Value?')
      (let [(vs (Struct_get s u))]
        (if (= (seq_length vs) 0)
          (opt 'Value?')
          (if (= (seq_length vs) 1)
            (opt 'Value?' (ith vs 0))
            (wrong "Repeated field: " u)))))

    (fn fanoutFields ((t SymTok) (vs 'Value*') -> 'Field*')
      (if (seq_is_empty vs)
        (seq 'Field*')
        (seq_prepend (tuple Field t (seq_head vs))
                     (fanoutFields t (seq_tail vs)))))


    //==========================================================================
    // Abstract Syntax Trees, which can contain unresolved SIDs

    (dom TSTree     = (+ STree IVM))
    (dom STree      = (+ SValue SEexp))
    (dom SValue     = (* 'SSymTok*'::annots SContent::content))
    (dom SContent   = (+ SSymbol SList SSexp SStruct NullNull Bool Int String
                         /*Decimal Float Timestamp Blob Clob*/))

    (dom SSymTok   = (+ Unicode I))
    (dom SSymbol   = (+ SSymTok DotNull))

    (dom SList     = (+ 'STree*' DotNull))
    (dom SSexp     = (+ 'STree*' DotNull))

    (dom SField    = (* SSymTok::name STree::tree))
    (dom SStruct   = (+ 'SField*' DotNull))

    (dom SEexp      = (* MacroRef::ref 'SEexpArg*'::args))

    // Distinguish between an individual arg and group of individual args.
    (dom SEexpArg   = (+ STree 'STree*'))

    // Absent module denotes a local ref like ':name' or ':12'.
    // When module="" it denotes a bare reference (no leading colon) inside
    // module bodies.  It cannot be resolved by E-expressions.
    (dom MacroRef   = (* 'Unicode?'::module NameOrAddr::macro))
    (dom NameOrAddr = (+ Unicode I))


    // Ion Version Markers

    (dom IVM = (* I I) "Ion version markers")

    (const IVM_1_0 (tuple IVM 1 0))
    (const IVM_1_1 (tuple IVM 1 1))

    (fn IVM_eq ((i1 IVM) (i2 IVM)-> B)
      (and (= (ith i1 0) (ith i2 0))
           (= (ith i1 1) (ith i2 1))))


    //==========================================================================
    // Parsing Interface

    // Here we abstract over the parser, to show the encoding feedback loop.
    // The parsing layer is given a subset of the expansion environment.
    // It would be easier to just pass the Environment, but this is explicit
    // WRT exactly what information can affect parsing.

    (dom ParseStep    = (* TSTree::tree ParseStream::next))
    (dom ParseStream  = (-> IVM 'ParseStep?'))

    (dom Document  = (^ is_truthy) "Ion documents")
    (dom Parser    = (-> Document ParseStream))


    //==========================================================================
    // Expansion of abstract syntax trees into values

    (dom Environment = (* Catalog::catalog
                          Module::sysModule
                          ModuleMap::modules
                          'SymTok*'::docSymbols
                          'Unicode*'::mactab))
    // docSymbols does not include $0 or system symbols


    (fn currentSpecVersion ((r Environment) -> IVM)
      (Module_specVersion (Environment_sysModule r)))

    (fn currentSymtab ((r Environment) -> 'SymTok*')
      (seq_prepend (lift_to SymTok SYM0)
                   (seq_append (Module_symtab (Environment_sysModule r))
                               (Environment_docSymbols r))))


    (dom ModuleMap = (-> Unicode Module))

    (fn emptyModuleMap ModuleMap (u)
      (wrong "Module not in scope: " u))

    (fn ModuleMap_extend ((mm ModuleMap) (u Unicode) (m Module) -> ModuleMap)
      (mk_fn ModuleMap (u1)
        (if (= u1 u) m
          (mm u1))))


    (fn expand_STree ((t STree) (r Environment) -> 'Value*')
      (if (element_of t SValue)
        (seq 'Value*' (expand_SValue (lower t SValue) r))
        (expand_SEexp (lower t SEexp) r)))

    (fn 'expand_STree*' ((ts 'STree*') (r Environment) -> 'Value*')
      (if (seq_is_empty ts)
        (seq 'Value*')
        (seq_append ('expand_STree'  (seq_head ts) r)
                    ('expand_STree*' (seq_tail ts) r))))

    (fn expand_SValue ((sv SValue) (r Environment) -> Value)
      (tuple Value ('expand_SSymTok*' (SValue_annots  sv) r)
                   ('expand_SContent' (SValue_content sv) r)))

    (fn expand_SContent ((sv SContent) (r Environment) -> Content)
      (if (element_of sv SSymbol)
        (lift (expand_SSymbol (lower sv SSymbol) r) Content)
        (if (element_of sv SList)
          (lift (expand_SList (lower sv SList) r) Content)
          (if (element_of sv SSexp)
            (lift (expand_SSexp (lower sv SSexp) r) Content)
            (if (element_of sv SStruct)
              (lift (expand_SStruct (lower sv SStruct) r) Content)
              (if (element_of sv NullNull)
                (lift (lower sv NullNull) Content)
                (if (element_of sv Bool)
                  (lift (lower sv Bool) Content)
                  (if (element_of sv Int)
                    (lift (lower sv Int) Content)
                    (if (element_of sv String)
                      (lift (lower sv String) Content)
                      (wrong "not implemented in this model"))))))))))


    // Symbol expansion

    (fn expand_SSymbol ((v SSymbol) (r Environment) -> Symbol)
      (if (element_of v DotNull)
        (lift DOTNULL Symbol)
        (lift (expand_SSymTok (lower v SSymTok) r) Symbol)))

    (fn expand_SSymTok ((s SSymTok) (r Environment) -> SymTok)
      (if (element_of s Unicode)
        (lift (lower s Unicode) SymTok)
        (let [(i  (lower s I)),
              (ts (currentSymtab r))]
          (if (< i (seq_length ts))
            (ith ts i)
            (wrong "Invalid symbol address " i)))))

    (fn 'expand_SSymTok*' ((ss 'SSymTok*') (r Environment) -> 'SymTok*')
      (if (seq_is_empty ss)
        EMPTY_SYMTOKS
        (seq_prepend (expand_SSymTok  (seq_head ss) r)
                     ('expand_SSymTok*' (seq_tail ss) r))))


    // Sequence expansion

    (fn expand_SList ((v SList) (r Environment) -> List)
      (if (element_of v DotNull)
        (lift DOTNULL List)
        (lift ('expand_STree*' (lower v 'STree*') r) List)))

    (fn expand_SSexp ((v SSexp) (r Environment) -> Sexp)
      (if (element_of v DotNull)
        (lift DOTNULL Sexp)
        (lift ('expand_STree*' (lower v 'STree*') r) Sexp)))


    // Struct expansion

    (fn expand_SStruct ((v SStruct) (r Environment) -> Struct)
      (if (element_of v DotNull)
        (lift DOTNULL Struct)
        (lift ('expand_SField*' (lower v 'SField*') r) Struct)))

    (fn expand_SField ((sf 'SField') (r Environment) -> 'Field*')
      (let [(t  (expand_SSymTok (SField_name sf) r)),
            (vs (expand_STree   (SField_tree sf) r))]
        (fanoutFields t vs)))

    (fn 'expand_SField*' ((sfs 'SField*') (r Environment) -> 'Field*')
      (if (seq_is_empty sfs)
        (seq 'Field*')
        (seq_append (expand_SField (seq_head sfs) r) ('expand_SField*' (seq_tail sfs) r))))


    //==========================================================================
    // Top-level evaluation

    (dom Evaluator = (-> Document Catalog 'Value*'))

    (fn mk_Evaluator ((p Parser) -> Evaluator)
      (mk_fn Evaluator (d c)
        (let [(p0 (p d)),
              (r0 (tuple Environment c (systemModule IVM_1_0)
                    emptyModuleMap
                    EMPTY_SYMTOKS
                    (seq 'Unicode*' /* No user macros installed */))),
              (k0 (mk_fn TContinuation (r vs) vs))]
          (TE_ParseStream p0 r0 k0))))


    (dom TContinuation = (-> Environment 'Value*' 'Value*')
      "Continuation when expanding top-level values")


    (fn TE_ParseStream ((p ParseStream) (r Environment) (k TContinuation) -> 'Value*')
      (let [(step (p (currentSpecVersion r)))]
        (if (opt_is_present step)
          (TE_TSTree (ParseStep_tree (opt_value step)) r
            (mk_fn TContinuation (r1 vs1)
              (TE_ParseStream (ParseStep_next (opt_value step)) r1
                (mk_fn TContinuation (r2 vs2)
                  (k r2 (seq_append vs1 vs2))))))
          (k r (seq 'Value*')))))


    (fn TE_TSTree ((t TSTree) (r Environment) (k TContinuation) -> 'Value*')
      (if (element_of t IVM)
        (k (compile_IVM (lower t IVM) r) (seq 'Value*'))
        (let [(vs (expand_STree (lower t STree) r))]
          ('TE_Value*' vs r k))))


    (fn TE_Value ((v Value) (r Environment) (k TContinuation) -> 'Value*')
      (if (isLocalSymbolTable v)
        (k (compile_LST (lower (Value_content v) Struct) r) (seq 'Value*'))
        (if (and (IVM_eq (currentSpecVersion r) IVM_1_1) (isIonLiteral v))
          (TE_literal v r k)
          (if (and (IVM_eq (currentSpecVersion r) IVM_1_1) (isEncodingDirective v))
            (k (compile_ED (lower (Value_content v) Sexp) r) (seq 'Value*'))
            (k r (seq 'Value*' v))))))

    (fn 'TE_Value*' ((vs 'Value*') (r Environment) (k TContinuation) -> 'Value*')
      (if (seq_is_empty vs)
        (k r vs)
        (TE_Value (seq_head vs) r
          (mk_fn TContinuation (r1 vs1)
            ('TE_Value*' (seq_tail vs) r1
              (mk_fn TContinuation (r2 vs2)
                (k r2 (seq_append vs1 vs2))))))))


    //==========================================================================
    // IVM compilation

    (fn compile_IVM ((i IVM) (r Environment) -> Environment)
      (tuple Environment
        (Environment_catalog r)
        (systemModule i)
        emptyModuleMap
        EMPTY_SYMTOKS
        (seq 'Unicode*' /* No user macros installed */)))


    //==========================================================================
    // $ion_symbol_table compilation

    (fn isLocalSymbolTable ((v Value) -> B)
      (and (element_of (Value_content v) Struct)
           (and (not (seq_is_empty (Value_annots v)))
                (SymTok_matches (seq_head (Value_annots v)) "$ion_symbol_table"))))

    (fn compile_LST ((s Struct) (r Environment) -> Environment)
      (if (element_of s DotNull)
        (compile_LST (lift (seq 'Field*') Struct) r)
        (let [(is (if ('Value?_is_symbol_matching'
                        ('hint:paren' (Struct_get1 s "imports"))
                        "$ion_symbol_table")
                    (Environment_docSymbols r)
                    (compile_LST_imports (normalize_list (Struct_get1 s "imports")) r))),
              (ss (map 'SymTok*' compile_LST_symbol
                    (normalize_list (Struct_get1 s "symbols"))))]
          (tuple Environment
            (Environment_catalog r)
            (Environment_sysModule r)
            emptyModuleMap
            (seq_append is ss)
            (seq 'Unicode*')))))


    // LST symbols field

    // Try inlining c for better math and collapsing ifs
    (fn normalize_list ((v 'Value?') -> 'Value*')
      (if (opt_is_present v)
        (let [(c (Value_content (opt_value v)))]
          ('hint:oneline'
            (if (and (element_of c List) (not (element_of c DotNull)))
              (lower c List 'Value*')
              (seq 'Value*'))))
        (seq 'Value*')))

    (fn compile_LST_symbol ((v Value) -> SymTok)
      (let [(c (Value_content v))]
        ('hint:oneline'
          (if (and (element_of c String) (not (element_of c DotNull)))
            (lift_to SymTok (lower c String Unicode))
            (lift_to SymTok SYM0)))))

    // LST imports field

    (fn compile_LST_imports ((vs 'Value*') (r Environment) -> 'SymTok*')
      // Would be nice to `map`, but this has two args and appends, not cons'es.
      // [FOLD] might do the trick.
      (if (seq_is_empty vs)
        EMPTY_SYMTOKS
        (let [(c (Value_content (seq_head vs)))]
          (let [(ts ('hint:oneline'
                      (if (and (element_of c Struct) (not (element_of c DotNull)))
                        (compile_import (lower c Struct) r)
                        EMPTY_SYMTOKS)))]
            (seq_append ts (compile_LST_imports (seq_tail vs) r))))))

    (fn compile_import ((s Struct) (r Environment) -> 'SymTok*')
      (let [(n (normalize_name    (Struct_get1 s "name"   ))),
            (v (normalize_version (Struct_get1 s "version"))),
            (m (normalize_max_id  (Struct_get1 s "max_id" )))]
        (if (or (= n "") (= n "$ion"))
          (seq 'SymTok*')
          (if (opt_is_present m)
            // We have max_id, find best-match and adjust the length
            (let [(mod (bestModule_Catalog (Environment_catalog r) n v))]
              (let [(ts ('hint:oneline'
                          (if (opt_is_present mod)
                            (Module_symtab (SharedModule_module (opt_value mod)))
                            (seq 'SymTok*'))))]
                (enforceMaxId ts n (opt_value m))))
            // No max_id, use exact match.
            (let [(mod (exactModule_Catalog (Environment_catalog r) n v))]
              (Module_symtab (SharedModule_module mod)))))))

    
    (fn enforceMaxId ((ts 'SymTok*') (moduleName Unicode) (maxId I) -> 'SymTok*')
      (let [(l (seq_length ts))]
        (if (< l maxId)
          (let [(t (lift (tuple AbsentSym moduleName (+ l 1)) SymTok))]
            (enforceMaxId (seq_append ts (seq 'SymTok*' t)) moduleName maxId))
          (if (> l maxId)
            (seq_truncate ts maxId)
            ts))))


    (fn normalize_name ((v 'Value?') -> Unicode)             // "" = absent or invalid
      (if (and (opt_is_present v)
               (and (element_of (Value_content (opt_value v)) String)
                    (not (element_of (Value_content (opt_value v)) DotNull))))
        (lower (Value_content (opt_value v)) String Unicode)
        ""))

    (fn normalize_version ((v 'Value?') -> I)                // 1 = absent or invalid
      (if (and (opt_is_present v)
               (and (element_of (Value_content (opt_value v)) Int)
                    (and (not (element_of (Value_content (opt_value v)) DotNull))
                         (>= (lower (Value_content (opt_value v)) Int I) 1))))
        (lower (Value_content (opt_value v)) Int I)
        1))

    (fn normalize_max_id ((v 'Value?') -> 'I?')              // <> = absent or invalid
      (if (and (opt_is_present v)
               (and (element_of (Value_content (opt_value v)) Int)
                    (and (not (element_of (Value_content (opt_value v)) DotNull))
                         (>= (lower (Value_content (opt_value v)) Int I) 0))))
        (opt 'I?' (lower (Value_content (opt_value v)) Int I))
        (opt 'I?')))


    //==========================================================================
    // Encoding Modules

    (dom Module        = (* IVM::specVersion 'SymTok*'::symtab 'ExportedMacro*'::mactab))
    (dom SharedModule  = (* Unicode::name I::version Module::module))


    //==========================================================================
    // Catalogs

    (dom Catalog = (* 'SharedModule*'::modules))


    (fn exactModule_Catalog ((c Catalog) (n Unicode) (v I) -> 'SharedModule')
      (exactModule_SMs (Catalog_modules c) n v))

    (fn exactModule_SMs ((ss 'SharedModule*') (n Unicode) (v I) -> 'SharedModule')
      (if (seq_is_empty ss)
        (wrong "No exact-match for " n "@" v)
        (if (and (= (SharedModule_name    (seq_head ss)) n)
                 (= (SharedModule_version (seq_head ss)) v))
          (seq_head ss)
          (exactModule_SMs (seq_tail ss) n v))))


    (fn bestModule_Catalog ((c Catalog) (n Unicode) (v I) -> 'SharedModule?')
      (bestModule_SMs (Catalog_modules c) n v))

    (fn bestModule_SMs ((ss 'SharedModule*') (n Unicode) (v I) -> 'SharedModule?')
      (if (seq_is_empty ss)
        (opt 'SharedModule?')
        // WARNING These variable names appear in the narrative, keep it in sync!
        (let [(ss1 (bestModule_SMs (seq_tail ss) n v))]
          (if (not (= (SharedModule_name (seq_head ss)) n))
            ss1
            (if (or (= (SharedModule_version (seq_head ss)) v)
                    (not (opt_is_present ss1)))
              // Exact match, or only match.
              (opt 'SharedModule?' (seq_head ss))
              // Inexact match, and the tail had a match.
              (if (or (= (SharedModule_version (opt_value ss1)) v)
                      (>  (SharedModule_version (opt_value ss1))
                          (SharedModule_version (seq_head ss))))
                // The tail had an exact match, or larger version.
                ss1
                (opt 'SharedModule?' (seq_head ss))))))))

    (fn Catalog_extend ((c Catalog) (s SharedModule) -> Catalog)
      // TODO reject duplicate key
      (tuple Catalog (seq_prepend s (Catalog_modules c))))


    //==========================================================================
    // System Modules

    (const systemSymbols_1_0
      ('hint:multiline'
        (seq 'Unicode*'
          "$ion"
          "$ion_1_0"
          "$ion_symbol_table"
          "name"
          "version"
          "imports"
          "symbols"
          "max_id"
          "$ion_shared_symbol_table")))


    (fn systemModule ((i IVM) -> Module)
      (if (IVM_eq i IVM_1_0)
        (tuple Module i (map 'SymTok*' inSymTok systemSymbols_1_0) (seq 'ExportedMacro*'))
        (if (IVM_eq i IVM_1_1)
          (tuple Module i (map 'SymTok*' inSymTok systemSymbols_1_1) systemMacros_1_1)
          (wrong "Unsupported Ion version: " (ith i 0) "." (ith i 1)))))


    //==========================================================================
    // Shared Symbol Table complation

    (fn isSST ((v Value) -> B)
      (and (element_of (Value_content v) Struct)
           (and (not (seq_is_empty (Value_annots v)))
              (SymTok_matches (seq_head (Value_annots v)) "$ion_shared_symbol_table"))))

    (fn compile_SST ((s Struct) -> SharedModule)
      (let [(n (normalize_name    (Struct_get1 s "name"))),
            // Yes, SST version is normalized to 1
            (v (normalize_version (Struct_get1 s "version"))),
            (s (normalize_list    (Struct_get1 s "symbols")))]
        (if (= n "")
          (wrong "SST has invalid name")
          (tuple SharedModule n v
            (tuple Module IVM_1_0
              (compile_SST_symbols s n 1)
              (seq 'ExportedMacro*'))))))

    (fn compile_SST_symbols ((vs 'Value*') (moduleName Unicode) (i I) -> 'SymTok*')
      (if (seq_is_empty vs)
        (seq 'SymTok*')
        (let [(c (Value_content (seq_head vs)))]
          (let [(s (if (and (element_of c String) (not (element_of c DotNull)))
                     (lift_to SymTok (lower c String Unicode))
                     (lift_to SymTok (tuple AbsentSym moduleName i))))]
          (seq_prepend s (compile_SST_symbols (seq_tail vs) moduleName (+ i 1)))))))


    //==========================================================================
    // Ion 1.1

    //==========================================================================
    // Literals

    (fn isIonLiteral ((v Value) -> B)
      (and (not (seq_is_empty (Value_annots v)))
           (SymTok_matches (seq_head (Value_annots v)) "$ion_literal")))

    (fn TE_literal ((v Value) (r Environment) (k TContinuation) -> 'Value*')
      (let [(v1 (tuple Value (seq_tail (Value_annots v)) (Value_content v)))]
        (if (isLocalSymbolTable v1)
          (wrong "Cannot use literal $ion_symbol_table struct as application data")
          (k r (seq 'Value*' v1)))))


    //==========================================================================
    // Macros

    // TODO:[MAC-ID] Retain original module name+version and macro NameOrAddr
    (dom Macro = (* Signature::signature Transform::xform))

    (dom Transform = (-> 'Value**' 'Value*'))

    (dom Signature   = (* 'ParamSpec*'::params 'RestSpec?'::rest /* TODO ResultSpec */))

    // TODO Should name be a SymTok?
    (dom ParamSpec   = (* Unicode::name ParamShape::shape))
    (dom RestSpec    = (* Unicode::name  RestShape::shape))

    (dom ParamShape  = (* ParamType::type Cardinality::card))
    (dom RestShape   = (* ParamType::type SeqCardinality::card))

    (dom ParamType   = (+ AbstractParamType Macro))

    // Not really happy with this but ANY is used in too many places right now.
    (dom AbstractParamType = (= _ANY))
    (const ANY (lift_to ParamType _ANY))

    (dom Cardinality    = (+ OptCardinality SeqCardinality))
    (dom OptCardinality = (= ZERO_OR_ONE  EXACTLY_ONE))
    (dom SeqCardinality = (= ZERO_OR_MORE ONE_OR_MORE))

    (fn Signature_vars ((s Signature) -> 'Unicode*')
      (seq_append
        (map 'Unicode*' ParamSpec_name (Signature_params s))
        (if (opt_is_present (Signature_rest s))
          (seq 'Unicode*' (RestSpec_name (opt_value (Signature_rest s))))
          (seq 'Unicode*'))))


    (fn is_voidable ((p ParamSpec) -> B)
      (is_voidable_Cardinality (ParamShape_card (ParamSpec_shape p))))

    (fn is_voidable_Cardinality ((c Cardinality) -> B)
      (or (and (element_of c OptCardinality)
               (= (lower c OptCardinality) ZERO_OR_ONE))
          (and (element_of c SeqCardinality)
               (= (lower c SeqCardinality) ZERO_OR_MORE))))


    (dom ExportedMacro = (* 'Unicode?'::name Macro::macro))


    (fn export ((name Unicode) (params 'ParamSpec*') (rest 'RestSpec?') (xform F) -> ExportedMacro)
      (tuple ExportedMacro (opt 'Unicode?' name)
        (tuple Macro (tuple Signature params rest) xform)))

    (const NO_REST (opt 'RestSpec?'))

    (fn 'param!' ((name Unicode) (type ParamType) -> ParamSpec)
      (tuple ParamSpec name
        (tuple ParamShape type (lift_to Cardinality EXACTLY_ONE))))

    (fn 'param*' ((name Unicode) (type ParamType) -> ParamSpec)
      (tuple ParamSpec name
        (tuple ParamShape type (lift_to Cardinality ZERO_OR_MORE))))

    (fn 'rest...' ((name Unicode) (type ParamType) -> 'RestSpec?')
      (opt 'RestSpec?' (tuple RestSpec name (tuple RestShape type ZERO_OR_MORE))))


    //==========================================================================
    // Macro Reference Resolution for Eexprs

    (fn resolve_MacroRef ((m MacroRef) (r Environment) -> Macro)
      (let [(mod (MacroRef_module m)),
            (mac (MacroRef_macro  m))]
        (if (opt_is_present mod)
          // Qualified reference
          (if (element_of mac Unicode)
            (resolve_qualifiedName (opt_value mod) (lower mac Unicode) (currentInstalledModuleMap r))
            (resolve_qualifiedAddr (opt_value mod) (lower mac I      ) (currentInstalledModuleMap r)))
          // Unqualified name or local-offset
          (if (element_of mac Unicode)
            (resolve_unqualifiedName (lower mac Unicode) r)
            (resolve_unqualifiedAddr (lower mac I      ) r)))))


    (fn currentInstalledModuleMap ((r Environment) -> ModuleMap)
      (mk_fn ModuleMap (u)
        (if (= u "$ion")
          (Environment_sysModule r)
          (letrec [(seek (lambda (modNames)
                           (if (seq_is_empty modNames)
                             (wrong "Module not in scope: " u)
                             (if (= (seq_head modNames) u)
                               ((Environment_modules r) u)
                               (seek (seq_tail modNames))))))]
            (seek (Environment_mactab r))))))


    // index is zero-based
    (fn resolve_qualifiedAddr ((u Unicode) (i I) (mm ModuleMap) -> Macro)
      (let [(ms (Module_mactab (mm u)))]
        (if (< i (seq_length ms))
          (ExportedMacro_macro (ith ms i))
          (wrong "Invalid macro address: :" u ":" i))))

    (fn resolve_qualifiedName ((u1 Unicode) (u2 Unicode) (mm ModuleMap) -> Macro)
      (let [(m (resolve_ExportedMacros (Module_mactab (mm u1)) u2))]
        (if (opt_is_present m)
          (opt_value m)
          (wrong "No such macro: :" u1 ":" u2))))

    // This assumes names are unique within the given sequence.
    (fn resolve_ExportedMacros ((ms 'ExportedMacro*') (u Unicode) -> 'Macro?')
      (if (seq_is_empty ms)
        (opt 'Macro?')
        (if (and (opt_is_present  (ExportedMacro_name (seq_head ms)))
                 (= (opt_value (ExportedMacro_name (seq_head ms))) u))
          (opt 'Macro?' (ExportedMacro_macro (seq_head ms)))
          (resolve_ExportedMacros (seq_tail ms) u))))


    (fn currentMacroStore ((r Environment) -> 'ExportedMacro*')
      (letrec [(join (lambda (mods)
                       (if (seq_is_empty mods)
                         (seq 'ExportedMacro*')
                         (seq_append (Module_mactab (seq_head mods))
                           (join (seq_tail mods))))))]
        (join (map 'Module*' (Environment_modules r) (Environment_mactab r)))))

    // index is zero-based; i0 is the original value
    (fn resolve_unqualifiedAddr ((i I) (r Environment) -> Macro)
      (let [(ms (currentMacroStore r))]
        (if (< i (seq_length ms))
          (ExportedMacro_macro (ith ms i))
          (wrong "Invalid macro address: :" i))))

    (fn resolve_unqualifiedName ((u Unicode) (r Environment) -> Macro)
      (let [(mods (map 'Module*' (Environment_modules r) (Environment_mactab r)))]
        (let [(m ('resolve_Module*' (seq_prepend (Environment_sysModule r) mods) u))]
          (if (opt_is_present m)
            (opt_value m)
            (wrong "No such macro: :" u)))))

    (fn 'resolve_Module*' ((mods 'Module*') (u Unicode) -> 'Macro?')
      (if (seq_is_empty mods)
        (opt 'Macro?')
        (let [(m1 (resolve_ExportedMacros (Module_mactab (seq_head mods)) u)),
              (m2 ('resolve_Module*'      (seq_tail mods) u))]
          (if (opt_is_present m1)
            // [MAC-ID] Compare macro identities to allow benign duplicates.
            (if (opt_is_present m2)
              (wrong "Ambiguous macro-ref: :" u)
              m1)
            m2))))


    //==========================================================================
    // Eexp Expansion

    (fn expand_SEexp ((v SEexp) (r Environment) -> 'Value*')
      (if (IVM_eq (currentSpecVersion r) IVM_1_0)
        (wrong "Eexp not allowed in Ion 1.0")
        (let [(m (resolve_MacroRef (SEexp_ref v) r))]
          (expand_macro m (SEexp_args v) r))))

    (fn expand_macro ((m Macro) (ts 'SEexpArg*') (r Environment) -> 'Value*')
      (let [(x (Macro_xform     m)),
            (s (Macro_signature m))]
        (x (expandArgs (Signature_params s) (Signature_rest s) r ts))))


    // Returns one Value* per parameter.
    // This should stay in sync with compileArgs
    (fn expandArgs ((ps 'ParamSpec*') (rest 'RestSpec?') (r Environment) (ts 'SEexpArg*') -> 'Value**')
      (if (seq_is_empty ps)
        (if (opt_is_present rest)
          // We have a rest-parameter, so grab everything that remains.
          (let [(t (RestShape_type (RestSpec_shape (opt_value rest)))),
                (c (lift_to Cardinality (RestShape_card (RestSpec_shape (opt_value rest)))))]
            (if (and (seq_is_empty ts) (not (is_voidable_Cardinality c)))
              (wrong "Too few arguments")
              (seq 'Value**' (validateShape t c (expandRest t ts r)))))
          (if (seq_is_empty ts)
            (seq 'Value**')                 // All done!
            (wrong "Too many arguments")))
        // More non-rest parameters to collate
        (let [(p (seq_head ps))]
          (if (seq_is_empty ts)
            // We hava a param, but no more arguments; param must be voidable.
            (if (is_voidable p)
              // No need to validateShape; we've done so statically.
              (seq_prepend (seq 'Value*')
                // Continue checking remaining parameters voidability
                (expandArgs (seq_tail ps) rest r ts))
              (wrong "Too few arguments"))
            // We have both a param and more arguments
            (let [(type (ParamShape_type (ParamSpec_shape p))),
                  (card (ParamShape_card (ParamSpec_shape p))),
                  (t    (seq_head ts))]                                    // ∈ SEexpArg
              (let [(vs (if (element_of t STree)
                          (expandArg   type (lower t  STree  ) r)
                          (if (not (and (element_of card OptCardinality)
                                        (= (lower card OptCardinality) EXACTLY_ONE)))
                            (expandGroup type (lower t 'STree*') r)
                            (wrong "Unexpected argument group"))))]
                // Separate `let` ensures args are expanded left-to-right.
                (let [(is (expandArgs (seq_tail ps) rest r (seq_tail ts)))]
                  // Type/cardinality validation of stream happens afterwards.
                  (seq_prepend (validateShape type card vs) is))))))))

    (fn expandArg ((t ParamType) (stx 'STree') (r Environment) -> 'Value*')
      (if (element_of t Macro)
        (if (element_of stx SValue)           // SValue ∈ STree ∈ SEexpArg
          // TODO reject annotations?
          (if (element_of (SValue_content (lower stx SValue)) SSexp)
            (expand_macro (lower t Macro)
                          // TODO handle null.sexp
                          (map 'SEexpArg*' inSEexpArg
                            (lower (SValue_content (lower stx SValue)) SSexp 'STree*'))
                          r)
            (wrong "Expected sexp with macro arguments"))
          (wrong "Expected sexp with macro arguments, found an eexp"))
        // TODO:[PARAM-TYPE] validate non-macro tagless shapes
        (expand_STree stx r)))

    (fn expandGroup ((t ParamType) (stxs 'STree*') (r Environment) -> 'Value*')
      (if (seq_is_empty stxs)
        (seq 'Value*')
        (seq_append (expandArg   t (seq_head stxs) r)
                    (expandGroup t (seq_tail stxs) r))))

    (fn expandRest ((t ParamType) (stxs 'SEexpArg*') (r Environment) -> 'Value*')
      (if (seq_is_empty stxs)
        (seq 'Value*')
        (let [(stx (seq_head stxs))]
          (if (element_of stx STree)
            (seq_append (expandArg  t (lower stx STree) r)
                        (expandRest t (seq_tail stxs) r))
            (wrong "Unexpected argument group")))))


    (fn validateShape ((t ParamType) (c Cardinality) (vs 'Value*') -> 'Value*')
      // TODO:[PARAM-TYPE]
      (if (element_of c OptCardinality)
        (if (> (seq_length vs) 1)
          (wrong "More than one value provided for parameter")
          (if (and (= (lower c OptCardinality) EXACTLY_ONE)
                   (= (seq_length vs) 0))
            (wrong "No value provided for parameter")
            vs))
        (if (and (= (lower c SeqCardinality) ONE_OR_MORE)
                 (= (seq_length vs) 0))
          (wrong "No value provided for parameter")
          // ZERO_OR_MORE is handled implicitly; it always passes.
          vs)))


    //==========================================================================
    // $ion_encoding compilation

    (fn isEncodingDirective ((v Value) -> B)
      (and (element_of (Value_content v) Sexp)
           (and (not (seq_is_empty (Value_annots v)))
                (SymTok_matches (seq_head (Value_annots v)) "$ion_encoding"))))

    (fn compile_ED ((s Sexp) (r Environment) -> Environment)
      // TODO Consider disallowing null.sexp
      (if (element_of s DotNull)
        (compile_ED_retain (seq 'Value*')     r)
        (compile_ED_retain (lower s 'Value*') r)))

    (fn compile_ED_retain ((vs 'Value*') (r Environment) -> Environment)
      // FIXME This is inconsistent with other cases where $ion isn't present
      //   ATM we only need it as a way to determine the specVersion.
      (let [(mm0 (ModuleMap_extend emptyModuleMap "$ion" (Environment_sysModule r)))]
        (if (nextClauseIs vs "retain")
          (let [(args (clauseBody (seq_head vs))),
                (mm1  (Environment_modules r))]
            (if (and (= (seq_length args) 1)
                     (Value_is_symbol_matching (seq_head args) "*"))
              (compile_ED_modules (seq_tail vs) mm1 r)
              // TODO [FOLD]
              (letrec [(retain (|vs1 mm| (if (seq_is_empty vs1)
                                           mm
                                           (retain (seq_tail vs1)
                                             (ModuleMap_extend mm
                                               (Value_symtext (seq_head vs1))
                                               (mm1 (Value_symtext (seq_head vs1))))))))]
                (compile_ED_modules (seq_tail vs) (retain args mm0) r))))
          (compile_ED_modules vs mm0 r))))

    (fn compile_ED_modules ((vs 'Value*') (avail ModuleMap) (r Environment) -> Environment)
      // TODO:[ED-USE] [IMPORT]
      (if (nextClauseIs vs "load")
        (compile_ED_modules (seq_tail vs)
          (compile_ED_load (clauseBody (seq_head vs)) avail (Environment_catalog r))
          r)
        (if (nextClauseIs vs "module")
          (compile_ED_modules (seq_tail vs)
            (compile_ED_module (clauseBody (seq_head vs)) avail (Environment_catalog r))
            r)
          // End of module-decls
          (compile_ED_symtab vs avail r))))

    // Same logic should be used for modules
    (fn compile_ED_symtab ((vs 'Value*') (avail ModuleMap) (r Environment) -> Environment)
      (if (nextClauseIs vs "symbol_table")
        (compile_ED_mactab (seq_tail vs) avail
          (compile_module_symtab (clauseBody (seq_head vs)) avail)
          r)
        (compile_ED_mactab vs avail (seq 'SymTok*') r)))

    (fn compile_ED_mactab ((vs 'Value*')
                           (avail ModuleMap)
                           (ts 'SymTok*')
                           (r Environment) -> Environment)
      (if (nextClauseIs vs "macro_table")
        (compile_ED_final (seq_tail vs) avail ts
          (compile_ED_mactab_body (clauseBody (seq_head vs)) avail)
          r)
        (compile_ED_final vs avail ts (seq 'Unicode*') r)))

    (fn compile_ED_final ((vs 'Value*')
                          (avail ModuleMap)
                          (ts 'SymTok*')
                          (us 'Unicode*')
                          (r Environment) -> Environment)
      (if (not (seq_is_empty vs))
        (wrong "Unexpected encoding clause: " (seq_head vs))
        (tuple Environment
          (Environment_catalog r)
          (Environment_sysModule r)
          avail
          ts
          us)))


    // $ion_encoding load

    // TODO Rename; this is also used by inner modules.
    (fn compile_ED_load ((vs 'Value*') (avail ModuleMap) (c Catalog) -> ModuleMap)
      (let [(name    (Value_symtext (ith vs 0))),                // [VALID-NAME]
            (catname (Value_strtext (ith vs 1))),
            (version (Value_int     (ith vs 2))),                // [LOAD-MAXID]
            // TODO:[VALID-FORM] ensure no extra arguments
           ]
        (ModuleMap_extend avail name
          (SharedModule_module (exactModule_Catalog c catname version)))))


    // $ion_encoding module

    (fn compile_ED_module ((vs 'Value*') (avail ModuleMap) (c Catalog) -> ModuleMap)
      (let [(name (Value_symtext (ith vs 0)))]                   // [VALID-NAME]
        (ModuleMap_extend avail name
          (compile_IM_body (seq_tail vs) avail c))))

    // $ion_encoding symbol_table

    (fn compile_module_symtab ((vs 'Value*') (avail ModuleMap) -> 'SymTok*')
      (if (seq_is_empty vs)
        (seq 'SymTok*')
        (seq_append (compile_module_symtab_elt (seq_head vs) avail)
          (compile_module_symtab (seq_tail vs) avail))))

    (fn compile_module_symtab_elt ((v Value) (avail ModuleMap) -> 'SymTok*')
      (if (element_of (Value_content v) Symbol)
        // TODO:[LOAD-MAXID] this assumes exact match acquired
        (Module_symtab (avail (Value_symtext v)))
        (map 'SymTok*' compile_module_symtab_text
          (lower (Value_content v) List 'Value*'))))

    (fn compile_module_symtab_text ((v Value) -> SymTok)
      // TODO:[ERRMSG] typecheck, nullcheck
      (lift_to SymTok (Value_strtext v)))


    (fn compile_ED_mactab_body ((vs 'Value*') (avail ModuleMap) -> 'Unicode*')
      (if (seq_is_empty vs)
        (seq 'Unicode*')
        // TODO [ERRMSG] Poor handling of null.symbol
        // We only compute `m` to verify the module reference is valid.
        (let [(m (avail (Value_symtext (seq_head vs))))]
          (seq_prepend (Value_symtext (seq_head vs))
            (compile_ED_mactab_body (seq_tail vs) avail)))))


    (fn nextClauseIs ((vs 'Value*') (u Unicode) -> B)
      (and (not (seq_is_empty vs))
           (isClause (seq_head vs) u)))

    (fn isClause ((v Value) (u Unicode) -> B)
      (and (element_of (Value_content v) Sexp)          // [ERRMSG] Null check v
        (and (not (seq_is_empty (lower (Value_content v) Sexp 'Value*')))
          (Value_is_symbol_matching (seq_head (lower (Value_content v) Sexp 'Value*')) u))))

    (fn clauseBody ((v Value) -> 'Value*')
      (seq_tail (lower (Value_content v) Sexp 'Value*')))


    //==========================================================================
    // Inline module compilation

    (fn compile_IM_body ((vs 'Value*') (avail ModuleMap) (c Catalog) -> Module)
      (compile_IM_deps vs avail c
        // The macro environment at the outside of an inline module includes
        // retained or loaded modules and used macro names.
        (mk_fn MacroEnv (mod mac)
          (if (not (opt_is_present mod))
            (wrong "local-ref should have been resolved already")
            (if (= (opt_value mod) "")
              // Bare reference; assume Unicode name, not address.
              // $ion is implicitly `use`d
              (let [(m1 (resolve_ExportedMacros (Module_mactab (avail "$ion"))
                                                (lower mac Unicode)))]
                (if (opt_is_present m1)
                  (opt_value m1)
                  (wrong "No such macro: " (lower mac Unicode))))
              // Qualified reference
              (if (element_of mac Unicode)
                (resolve_qualifiedName (opt_value mod) (lower mac Unicode) avail)
                (resolve_qualifiedAddr (opt_value mod) (lower mac I      ) avail)))))))


    (fn compile_IM_deps ((vs 'Value*') (avail ModuleMap) (c Catalog) (r MacroEnv) -> Module)
      // TODO:[IMPORT]
      (if (nextClauseIs vs "load")
        // Recurse to find more dependencies
        (compile_IM_deps (seq_tail vs)
          (compile_ED_load (clauseBody (seq_head vs)) avail c)
          c
          r) // [LOAD-MACRO] loaded module needs to be visibile in this MacroEnv
        (if (nextClauseIs vs "use")
          (compile_IM_use (clauseBody (seq_head vs)) (seq_tail vs) c avail r)
          // No more dependencies
          (compile_IM_symtab vs avail r))))

    // Use-clauses make macros available for bare-name reference.
    (fn compile_IM_use ((vs 'Value*')     // The rest of this `use` clause
                        (vs1 'Value*')    // The rest of the IM body
                        (c Catalog)
                        (avail ModuleMap)
                        (r MacroEnv) -> Module)
      (if (seq_is_empty vs)
        (compile_IM_deps vs1 avail c r)
        // TODO:[USE-LOAD] Accept nested `load` clause.
        // Resolve the module reference immediately
        (let [(mod0 (avail (Value_symtext (seq_head vs))))]  // [ERRMSG]
          (compile_IM_use (seq_tail vs) vs1 c avail
            (mk_fn MacroEnv (mod1 mac)
              (if (not (opt_is_present mod1))
                (wrong "local-ref should have been resolved already")
                (if (= (opt_value mod1) "")
                  // Bare name
                  (let [(m1 (resolve_ExportedMacros (Module_mactab mod0)
                                                    (lower mac Unicode)))]
                    (if (opt_is_present m1)
                      (if (is_bottom (r mod1 mac))
                        (opt_value m1)
                        // [MAC-ID] Compare macro identities to allow benign duplicates.
                       (wrong "Ambiguous macro-ref: " (lower mac Unicode)))
                      // Not introduced by this use-clause, so keep looking.
                      (r mod1 mac)))
                  // Qualified reference; pass through.
                  (r mod1 mac))))))))

    (fn compile_IM_symtab ((vs 'Value*') (avail ModuleMap) (r MacroEnv) -> Module)
      (if (nextClauseIs vs "symbol_table")
        (compile_IM_mactab (seq_tail vs) avail r
          (compile_module_symtab (clauseBody (seq_head vs)) avail))
        (compile_IM_mactab vs avail r (seq 'SymTok*'))))

    // TODO:[ALIAS]

    (fn compile_IM_mactab ((vs 'Value*')
                           (avail ModuleMap)
                           (r     MacroEnv)
                           (ts 'SymTok*') -> Module)
      (if (nextClauseIs vs "macro_table")
        (compile_IM_final (seq_tail vs) avail ts
          (compile_module_mactab (clauseBody (seq_head vs)) avail r (seq 'ExportedMacro*')))
        (compile_IM_final vs avail ts (seq 'ExportedMacro*'))))

    (fn compile_IM_final ((vs 'Value*')
                          (avail ModuleMap)
                          (ts 'SymTok*')
                          (ms 'ExportedMacro*') -> Module)
      (if (not (seq_is_empty vs))
        (wrong "Unexpected clause in module: " (seq_head vs))
        (tuple Module (Module_specVersion (avail "$ion")) ts ms)))


    (fn compile_module_mactab ((vs   'Value*')
                               (mods ModuleMap)
                               (r    MacroEnv)
                               (macs 'ExportedMacro*') -> 'ExportedMacro*')
      (if (seq_is_empty vs)
        macs
        (compile_module_mactab (seq_tail vs) mods r
          (compile_IM_mactab_elt (seq_head vs) mods r macs))))

    (fn compile_IM_mactab_elt ((v    Value)
                               (mods ModuleMap)
                               (r    MacroEnv)
                               (macs 'ExportedMacro*') -> 'ExportedMacro*')
      (if (isClause v "macro")
        (let [(macroEnv (localMacroEnv r macs))]
          (seq_append macs
            (seq 'ExportedMacro*' (compile_macro_defn (clauseBody v) mods macroEnv))))
        // TODO:[EXPORT-REF] (export foo ':$ion:foo')
        // TODO:[EXPORT-MOD] A plain module-name in place of (export ...)
        // TODO:[EXPORT-FROM] (export (from MODNAME ...))
        (let [(mod (mods (Value_symtext v)))]
          // [DUPE-NAME] Check for duplicates
          (seq_append macs (Module_mactab mod)))))

    // Create a MacroEnv that can resolve local names/addrs within a module.
    // Note that local macros shadow imported names.
    (fn localMacroEnv ((r MacroEnv) (ms 'ExportedMacro*') -> MacroEnv)
      // [DUPE-NAME] We assume no duplicate names in `ms`
      (mk_fn MacroEnv (mod mac)
        (if (opt_is_present mod)
          (if (= (opt_value mod) "")
            // Template uses a bare macro name, eg (make_string ...)
            (let [(m (resolve_ExportedMacros ms (lower mac Unicode)))]
               (if (opt_is_present m)
                 // Found the name locally; this shadows any import.
                 (opt_value m)
                 // Not a local macro; pass through to check `use`d modules.
                 (r mod mac)))
            // Qualified reference with real module name; pass through.
            (r mod mac))
          // Local name or offset
          (if (element_of mac Unicode)
            (let [(m (resolve_ExportedMacros ms (lower mac Unicode)))]
               (if (opt_is_present m)
                 (opt_value m)
                 (wrong "No such macro declared in this module: :" (lower mac Unicode))))
            (let [(i (lower mac I))]
              (if (< i (seq_length ms))
                (ExportedMacro_macro (ith ms i))
                (wrong "Invalid macro address: :" i)))))))


    //==========================================================================
    // Signature compilation

    (fn compile_Signature ((v Value) (r MacroEnv) -> Signature)
      (compile_Signature_params (Value_seqElements v) r))

    (fn compile_Signature_params ((ps 'Value*') (r MacroEnv) -> Signature)
      (if (seq_is_empty ps)
        (tuple Signature (seq 'ParamSpec*') NO_REST)
        (if (seq_is_empty (seq_tail ps))
          // Last entry, so it can be a rest-spec
          (if (isRestSpec (seq_head ps))
            (tuple Signature (seq 'ParamSpec*') (opt 'RestSpec?' (compile_restSpec (seq_head ps) r)))
            (tuple Signature (seq 'ParamSpec*' (compile_paramSpec (seq_head ps) r)) NO_REST))
          // ELSE there are >1 entries to handle, head cannot be rest-spec
          (let [(s (compile_Signature_params (seq_tail ps) r))]
            (tuple Signature
              (seq_prepend (compile_paramSpec (seq_head ps) r) (Signature_params s))
              (Signature_rest s))))))

    (fn isRestSpec ((v Value) -> B)
      (and (element_of (Value_content v) Sexp)
        (let [(vs (lower (Value_content v) Sexp 'Value*'))]
          (let [(i (- (seq_length vs) 1))]
            // We can't use functional `and`; it will run `ith` with bad index.
            (if (or (= i 1) (= i 2))
              // The LaTeX printer can't render `ith` with a complex index.
              (or (Value_is_symbol_matching (ith vs i) "...")
                  (Value_is_symbol_matching (ith vs i) "...+"))
              false)))))

    (fn compile_paramSpec ((v Value) (r MacroEnv) -> ParamSpec)
      (if (element_of (Value_content v) Symbol)
        (compile_paramType (seq 'Value*') (compile_paramName v) r)
        // [ERRMSG] Handle non-sexp, null.sexp
        (let [(vs (lower (Value_content v) Sexp 'Value*'))]
          (if (seq_is_empty vs)
            (wrong "Malformed param-spec: " v)
            (compile_paramType (seq_tail vs) (compile_paramName (seq_head vs)) r)))))

    (fn compile_paramType ((vs 'Value*') (u Unicode) (r MacroEnv) -> ParamSpec)
      (if (seq_is_empty vs)
        (compile_paramCard vs u ANY)
        (if (element_of (Value_content (seq_head vs)) Symbol)
          (let [(u1 (Value_symtext (seq_head vs)))]
            (if (looksLikeMacroRef u1) // Type keywords "look like" bare macro-ref
              // TODO:[PARAM-TYPE] Check for 'any' et al before treating as macro
              (let [(m (interp_macroref (seq_head vs) r))]
                (compile_paramCard (seq_tail vs) u (lift_to ParamType m)))
              (compile_paramCard vs u ANY)))
          (wrong "Unexpected element in param-spec: " (seq_head vs)))))

    (fn compile_paramCard ((vs 'Value*') (u Unicode) (t ParamType) -> ParamSpec)
      (if (seq_is_empty vs)
        (finishParamSpec vs u t (lift EXACTLY_ONE Cardinality))
        (if (Value_is_symbol_matching (seq_head vs) "!")
          (finishParamSpec (seq_tail vs) u t (lift EXACTLY_ONE Cardinality))
          (if (Value_is_symbol_matching (seq_head vs) "?")
            (finishParamSpec (seq_tail vs) u t (lift ZERO_OR_ONE Cardinality))
            (if (Value_is_symbol_matching (seq_head vs) "+")
              (finishParamSpec (seq_tail vs) u t (lift ONE_OR_MORE Cardinality))
              (if (Value_is_symbol_matching (seq_head vs) "*")
                (finishParamSpec (seq_tail vs) u t (lift ZERO_OR_MORE Cardinality))
                (wrong "Unexpected element in param-spec: " (seq_head vs))))))))

    (fn finishParamSpec ((vs 'Value*') (u Unicode) (t ParamType) (c Cardinality) -> ParamSpec)
      (if (seq_is_empty vs)
        (tuple ParamSpec u (tuple ParamShape t c))
        (wrong "Unexpected element in param-spec: " (seq_head vs))))


    (fn compile_restSpec ((v Value) (r MacroEnv) -> RestSpec)
      (let [(vs (lower (Value_content v) Sexp 'Value*'))]
        // We already checked length in isRestSpec
        (compile_restType (seq_tail vs) (compile_paramName (seq_head vs)) r)))

    (fn compile_restType ((vs 'Value*') (u Unicode) (r MacroEnv) -> RestSpec)
      (if (element_of (Value_content (seq_head vs)) Symbol)
        (let [(u1 (Value_symtext (seq_head vs)))]
          (if (looksLikeMacroRef u1) // Type keywords "look like" bare macro-ref
            // TODO:[PARAM-TYPE] Check for 'any' et al before treating as macro
            (let [(m (interp_macroref (seq_head vs) r))]
              (compile_restCard (seq_tail vs) u (lift_to ParamType m)))
            (compile_restCard vs u ANY)))
        (wrong "Unexpected element in rest-spec: " (seq_head vs))))

    (fn compile_restCard ((vs 'Value*') (u Unicode) (t ParamType) -> RestSpec)
      (if (Value_is_symbol_matching (seq_head vs) "...")
        (finishRestSpec (seq_tail vs) u t ZERO_OR_MORE)
        (if (Value_is_symbol_matching (seq_head vs) "...+")
          (finishRestSpec (seq_tail vs) u t ONE_OR_MORE)
          (wrong "Unexpected element in rest-spec: " (seq_head vs)))))

    (fn finishRestSpec ((vs 'Value*') (u Unicode) (t ParamType) (c SeqCardinality) -> RestSpec)
      (if (seq_is_empty vs)
        (tuple RestSpec u (tuple RestShape t c))
        (wrong "Unexpected element in rest-spec: " (seq_head vs))))


    (fn compile_paramName ((v Value) -> Unicode)
      // [VALID-NAME]
      (lower (Value_content v) Symbol SymTok Unicode))


    //==========================================================================
    // Macro definition compilation

    // Need ModuleMap, Environment_mactab module names, local and use'd macro map
    // As noted at MacroRef, an empty module name denotes a bare reference
    // (foo ...) as distinct from named locals (':foo' ...) where the module name
    // is absent.
    (dom MacroEnv = (-> 'Unicode?' NameOrAddr Macro))

    // The difference between Transform and Interpreter lies solely in their
    // inputs.
    //   * Transform inputs are the argument-streams from the macro
    //     invocation, one stream per parameter.
    //   * Interpreter inputs are the streams for all visible variables, with
    //     most recently introduced variables first, and parameters last.
    //     These bindings and positions are tracked by the `scope` sequence
    //     threaded through macro compilation.
    (dom Interpreter = (-> 'Value**' 'Value*'))

    (fn compile_macro_defn ((vs   'Value*')
                            (mods ModuleMap)
                            (macroEnv MacroEnv) -> ExportedMacro)
      // TODO:[VALID-FORM] check arity of this (macro ...) clause
      // TODO [OPT-NAME] [VALID-NAME] [DUPE-NAME]
      (let [(name  (Value_symtext (ith vs 0))),
            (sig   (compile_Signature (ith vs 1) macroEnv))]
        (tuple ExportedMacro (opt 'Unicode?' name)
          (tuple Macro sig (compile_xform (ith vs 2) sig macroEnv)))))

    (fn compile_xform ((v Value) (s Signature) (macroEnv MacroEnv) -> Transform)
      // Transforms are invoked after arity checking and argument collation, so we
      // can assume the correct number of streams (per the Signature) are given.
      (let [(i (interp_template v (Signature_vars s) macroEnv))]
        (mk_fn Transform (args)
          (i args))))

    // TODO:[DUPE-NAME] We assume all parameter names are unique


    (fn interp_template ((v Value) (scope 'Unicode*') (macroEnv MacroEnv) -> Interpreter)
      (if (element_of (Value_content v) Symbol)
        (interp_ref v scope)
        (if (element_of (Value_content v) List)
          (interp_list v scope macroEnv)
          (if (element_of (Value_content v) Struct)
            (interp_struct v scope macroEnv)
            (if (element_of (Value_content v) Sexp)
              (interp_sexp v scope macroEnv)
              (interp_literal v))))))

    (fn 'interp_template*' ((vs 'Value*') (scope 'Unicode*') (macroEnv MacroEnv) -> 'Interpreter*')
      (if (seq_is_empty vs)
        (seq 'Interpreter*')
        (seq_prepend (interp_template    (seq_head vs) scope macroEnv)
                     ('interp_template*' (seq_tail vs) scope macroEnv))))

    // Interpret multiple templates whose expansions are concatenated.
    (fn 'interp_template...' ((vs 'Value*') (scope 'Unicode*') (r MacroEnv) -> Interpreter)
      (let [(is ('interp_template*' vs scope r))]
        (mk_fn Interpreter (env)
          (letrec [(combine (lambda (is1)                              // [FOLD]
                              (if (seq_is_empty is1)
                                (seq 'Value*')
                                (seq_append ((seq_head is1) env)
                                            (combine (seq_tail is1))))))]
             (combine is)))))


    (fn interp_literal ((v Value) -> Interpreter)
      (mk_fn Interpreter (env)
        (seq 'Value*' v)))

    (fn resolve_ref ((v Value) (scope 'Unicode*') -> I)
      (let [(u (Value_symtext v))]  // Rejects $0, null, unknown
        (if (seq_is_empty scope)
         (wrong "Unbound variable: " u)
         (if (= (seq_head scope) u) 0
           (+ 1 (resolve_ref v (seq_tail scope)))))))

    (fn interp_ref ((v Value) (scope 'Unicode*') -> Interpreter)
      (let [(i (resolve_ref v scope))]
        (mk_fn Interpreter (env)
          (ith env i))))


    (fn interp_list ((v Value) (scope 'Unicode*') (macroEnv MacroEnv) -> Interpreter)
      (if (element_of (Value_content v) DotNull)
        (interp_literal v)
        (let [(us (Value_annots v)),
              (i ('interp_template...' (lower (Value_content v) List 'Value*') scope macroEnv))]
          (mk_fn Interpreter (env)
            (seq 'Value*' (tuple Value us (lift (i env) List Content)))))))

    (fn interp_struct ((v Value) (scope 'Unicode*') (macroEnv MacroEnv) -> Interpreter)
      (if (element_of (Value_content v) DotNull)
        (interp_literal v)
        (let [(us (Value_annots v)),
              (fs (lower (Value_content v) Struct 'Field*'))]
          (let [(ns (map 'SymTok*' Field_name fs)),
                (is (map 'Interpreter*' (lambda (f) (interp_template (Field_value f) scope macroEnv)) fs))]
            (mk_fn Interpreter (env)
              (letrec [(loop (lambda (ns1 is1)
                               (if (seq_is_empty ns1)
                                 (seq 'Field*')
                                 (seq_append
                                   (fanoutFields (seq_head ns1) ((seq_head is1) env))
                                   (loop (seq_tail ns1) (seq_tail is1))))))]
                (seq 'Value*' (tuple Value us (lift (loop ns is) Struct Content)))))))))


    (fn interp_sexp ((v Value) (scope 'Unicode*') (macroEnv MacroEnv) -> Interpreter)
      // TODO Treat null.sexp as a literal.
      (if (isClause v "literal")
        (interpSF_literal (clauseBody v) scope)
        (if (isClause v "if_void")
          (interpSF_if_void (clauseBody v) scope macroEnv)
          (if (isClause v "if_single")
            (interpSF_if_single (clauseBody v) scope macroEnv)
            (if (isClause v "if_multi")
              (interpSF_if_multi (clauseBody v) scope macroEnv)
              (if (isClause v "for")
                (interpSF_for (clauseBody v) scope macroEnv)
                (let [(vs (Value_seqElements v))]
                  (if (not (seq_is_empty vs))
                    (let [(m (interp_macroref (seq_head vs) macroEnv))]
                      (interp_macro (clauseBody v) m scope macroEnv))
                    (wrong "Malformed template: " v)))))))))


    // Special forms

    (fn interpSF_literal ((vs 'Value*') (scope 'Unicode*') -> Interpreter)
      (if (= (seq_length vs) 1)
        (mk_fn Interpreter (env) (seq 'Value*' (seq_head vs)))
        (wrong "Malformed literal clause")))

    (fn interpSF_if_void ((vs 'Value*') (scope 'Unicode*') (macroEnv MacroEnv) -> Interpreter)
      (if (= (seq_length vs) 3)
        (let [(is ('interp_template*' vs scope macroEnv))]
          (mk_fn Interpreter (env)
            (if (seq_is_empty ((ith is 0) env))
             ((ith is 1) env)
             ((ith is 2) env))))
        (wrong "Malformed if_void form")))

    (fn interpSF_if_single ((vs 'Value*') (scope 'Unicode*') (macroEnv MacroEnv) -> Interpreter)
      (if (= (seq_length vs) 3)
        (let [(is ('interp_template*' vs scope macroEnv))]
          (mk_fn Interpreter (env)
            (if (= (seq_length ((ith is 0) env)) 1)
             ((ith is 1) env)
             ((ith is 2) env))))
        (wrong "Malformed if_single form")))

    (fn interpSF_if_multi ((vs 'Value*') (scope 'Unicode*') (macroEnv MacroEnv) -> Interpreter)
      (if (= (seq_length vs) 3)
        (let [(is ('interp_template*' vs scope macroEnv))]
          (mk_fn Interpreter (env)
            (if (> (seq_length ((ith is 0) env)) 1)
             ((ith is 1) env)
             ((ith is 2) env))))
        (wrong "Malformed if_multi form")))

    (fn interpSF_for ((vs 'Value*') (scope 'Unicode*') (macroEnv MacroEnv) -> Interpreter)
      (if (= (seq_length vs) 2)
        (let [(bindings (Value_listElements (ith vs 0)))]
          (let [(us (map 'Unicode*' (lambda (b)
                                      (let [(vs1 (Value_seqElements b))]
                                        (if (= (seq_length vs1) 2)
                                          (Value_symtext (ith vs1 0))
                                          (wrong "Malformed `for` binding pair"))))
                      bindings)),
                (is ('interp_template*' (map 'Value*' (|b| (ith (Value_seqElements b) 1))
                                                      bindings)
                                        scope
                                        macroEnv))]
            // [DUPE-NAME] Reject duplicate entries in `us`
            (let [(i_body (interp_template (ith vs 1) (seq_append us scope) macroEnv))]
              (mk_fn Interpreter (env)
                (let [(as (map 'Value**' (lambda (i) (i env)) is))]
                  (letrec [(loop (lambda (streams)
                                   (let [(next (for_next_bindings streams))]
                                     (if (seq_is_empty next)
                                       (seq 'Value*')
                                       (seq_append (i_body (seq_append next env))
                                                   (loop (map 'Value**' seq_tail streams)))))))]
                    (loop as)))))))
        (wrong "Malformed `for` form")))

    (fn any_is_empty ((vss 'Value**') -> B)
      (if (seq_is_empty vss) false
        (or (seq_is_empty (seq_head vss))
            (any_is_empty (seq_tail vss)))))

    (fn for_next_bindings ((vss 'Value**') -> 'Value**')
      (if (any_is_empty vss)
        (seq 'Value**')
        (map 'Value**' (|s| (seq 'Value*' (seq_head s))) vss)))


    //==========================================================================
    // TL Macro invocation

    // TODO Reconsider where parameter-shape validation happens.
    // Currently it's happening at the macro call-site, but probably should
    // happen inside the macro-level Interpreter.
    //   * The call site needs to know some aspects, notably template-shapes
    //     (I think!) and optional/rest arguments for arity checkyng

    (fn Interpret_void Interpreter (env)
      (seq 'Value*'))

    (fn interp_macro ((vs 'Value*') (m Macro) (scope 'Unicode*') (r MacroEnv) -> Interpreter)
      (let [(f (Macro_xform     m)),
            (s (Macro_signature m))]
        (let [(is (compileArgs (Signature_params s) (Signature_rest s) scope r vs))]
          (mk_fn Interpreter (env)
            (let [(as (map 'Value**' (lambda (i) (i env)) is))]
              (f as))))))

    // TODO Not a great name; doesn't return Interpreter and we'll use this elsewhere.
    (fn interp_macroref ((v Value) (r MacroEnv) -> Macro)
      (let [(m (parseMacroRef (Value_symtext v)))]
        (let [(mod (MacroRef_module m)),
              (mac (MacroRef_macro  m))]
          (r mod mac))))

    // Returns one Interpreter per parameter.
    // This should stay in sync with expandArgs
    (fn compileArgs ((ps 'ParamSpec*') (rest 'RestSpec?') (scope 'Unicode*') (r MacroEnv) (vs 'Value*') -> 'Interpreter*')
      (if (seq_is_empty ps)
        (if (opt_is_present rest)
          // We have a rest-parameter, so grab all remaining templates.
          (let [(type (RestShape_type (RestSpec_shape (opt_value rest)))),
                (card (lift_to Cardinality (RestShape_card (RestSpec_shape (opt_value rest)))))]
            (if (and (seq_is_empty vs) (not (is_voidable_Cardinality card)))
              (wrong "Too few arguments")
              (let [(i (compileGroup vs type scope r))]
                (seq 'Interpreter*'
                  (mk_fn Interpreter (env)
                    (validateShape type card (i env)))))))
          (if (seq_is_empty vs)
            (seq 'Interpreter*')                 // All done!
            (wrong "Too many arguments")))
        // More non-rest parameters to collate
        (let [(p (seq_head ps))]
          (if (seq_is_empty vs)
            // We hava a param, but no more arguments; param must be voidable.
            (if (is_voidable p)
              (seq_prepend Interpret_void
                // No need to validateShape; we've done so statically.
                (compileArgs (seq_tail ps) rest scope r vs))
              (wrong "Too few arguments"))
            // We have both a param and more arguments
            (let [(type (ParamShape_type (ParamSpec_shape p))),
                  (card (ParamShape_card (ParamSpec_shape p))),
                  (v    (seq_head vs))]
              (let [(i (if (isClause v ";")
                          (if (not (and (element_of card OptCardinality)
                                        (= (lower card OptCardinality) EXACTLY_ONE)))
                            (compileGroup (clauseBody v) type scope r)
                            (wrong "Unexpected argument group"))
                         (compileArg v type scope r)))]
                // Separate `let` ensures args are expanded left-to-right.
                (let [(is (compileArgs (seq_tail ps) rest scope r (seq_tail vs)))]
                  (seq_prepend
                    (mk_fn Interpreter (env)
                      (validateShape type card (i env)))
                    is))))))))

    (fn compileArg ((v Value) (type ParamType) (scope 'Unicode*') (r MacroEnv) -> Interpreter)
      (if (element_of type Macro)
        // TODO:[TL-MACRO] support macro shapes
        (wrong "TL macro shapes not implemented")
        (interp_template v scope r)))

    // Like interp_template... but each element is shaped by the parameter type.
    (fn compileGroup ((vs 'Value*') (type ParamType) (scope 'Unicode*') (r MacroEnv) -> Interpreter)
      (if (seq_is_empty vs)
        Interpret_void
        (if (isClause (seq_head vs) ";")
          (wrong "Unexpected argument group")
          (let [(i  (compileArg   (seq_head vs) type scope r)),
                (is (compileGroup (seq_tail vs) type scope r))]
            (mk_fn Interpreter (env)
              (seq_append (i env) (is env)))))))


    //==========================================================================
    // System Module 1.1

    (const systemSymbols_1_1
      (seq_append systemSymbols_1_0
        (seq 'Unicode*'
          "$ion_literal"
          /* ... */)))

    // TODO We should produce these signatures by parsing from text.
    (const systemMacros_1_1
      ('hint:multiline'
        (seq 'ExportedMacro*'
          (export "void"
            (seq 'ParamSpec*')
            ('rest...' "args" ANY)
            (mk_fn Transform (rest)
              (seq 'Value*')))
          (export "values"
            (seq 'ParamSpec*')
            ('rest...' "args" ANY)
            (mk_fn Transform (args)
              (ith args 0)))
          (export "make_string"
            (seq 'ParamSpec*')
            ('rest...' "content" ANY)
            (mk_fn Transform (args)
              (seq 'Value*'
                (tuple Value (seq 'SymTok*')
                  (lift (appendText (ith args 0)) String Content)))))
          (export "make_symbol"
            (seq 'ParamSpec*')
            ('rest...' "content" ANY)
            (mk_fn Transform (args)
              (seq 'Value*'
                (tuple Value (seq 'SymTok*')
                  (lift (appendText (ith args 0)) SymTok Symbol Content)))))
          (export "make_list"
            (seq 'ParamSpec*')
            ('rest...' "args" ANY)
            (mk_fn Transform (args)
              (seq 'Value*'
                (tuple Value (seq 'SymTok*')
                  (lift_to Content (lift_to List (ith args 0)))))))
          (export "make_sexp"
            (seq 'ParamSpec*')
            ('rest...' "args" ANY)
            (mk_fn Transform (args)
              (seq 'Value*'
                (tuple Value (seq 'SymTok*')
                  (lift_to Content (lift_to Sexp (ith args 0)))))))
          (export "annotate"
            (seq 'ParamSpec*'
              ('param*' "anns"  ANY)
              ('param!' "value" ANY))
            (opt 'RestSpec?')
            (mk_fn Transform (args)
              (let [(ts (map 'SymTok*'
                            (lambda (v) // Value -> SymTok
                              (let [(c (Value_content v))]
                                (if (element_of c Symbol)
                                  (if (element_of c Unicode)
                                    (lower c Symbol SymTok)
                                    (wrong ":$ion:annotate doesn't accept null.symbol"))
                                  (if (element_of c String)
                                    (if (element_of c Unicode)
                                      (lift (lower c String Unicode) SymTok)
                                      (wrong ":$ion:annotate doesn't accept null.string"))
                                    (wrong "Not a text value")))))
                            (ith args 0)))]
                (seq 'Value*'
                  (tuple Value
                    (seq_append ts (Value_annots (seq_head (ith args 1))))
                    (Value_content (seq_head (ith args 1))))))))
          /* ... */)))


    (fn appendText ((vs 'Value*') -> Unicode)
      (if (seq_is_empty vs)
        (inject_into Unicode "")
        (Unicode_append (Value_unicode (seq_head vs))
          (appendText (seq_tail vs)))))

    (fn Value_unicode ((v Value) -> Unicode)
      // Turns null.string and null.symbol into ""
      (let [(c (Value_content v))]
        (if (element_of c Symbol)
          (if (element_of c Unicode)
            (lower c Symbol SymTok Unicode)
            "")
          (if (element_of c String)
            (if (element_of c Unicode)
              (lower c String Unicode)
              "")
            (wrong "Not a text value")))))
  )

  (define EMPTY_SYMTOKS    (seq 'SymTok*'))

  // [CTORS] These should be auto-generated; we need one-arg fn to use with `map`.
  (define (inSymTok v)
    (lift_to SymTok v))
  // TODO Latex rendering
  (define (inSEexpArg v)
    (lift_to SEexpArg v))


  // Be very selective with what is required! This escapes the denotational model.
  (require
    (only_in "/fusioncontrib/denotation"
      eject)
    (only_in "/fusioncontrib/denotation/private/util"
      string_holds_decimal_int
      string_holds_ion_identifier))

  (define_fn looksLikeMacroRef ((u Unicode) -> B)
    (or (string_holds_ion_identifier (eject u))
        (string_starts_with (eject u) ":")))

  (define_fn parseMacroRef ((c Unicode) -> MacroRef)
    (if (string_ends_with (eject c) ":")
      // Hack to workaround string_split igoring leading/trailing delimiters
      (wrong "Malformed macro-ref: " (eject c))
      (if (string_starts_with (eject c) ":")
        (let [(parts (string_split (eject c) ":"))]
          (if (= 1 (size parts))
            // Local reference
            (tuple MacroRef
              (opt 'Unicode?')
              (parseNameOrAddr c (. parts 0)))
            (if (= 2 (size parts))
              // Qualified reference
              (tuple MacroRef
                (opt 'Unicode?' (parseName c (. parts 0)))
                (parseNameOrAddr c (. parts 1)))
              // Too many parts
              (wrong "Malformed macro-ref: " (eject c)))))
        // Bare name
        (tuple MacroRef (opt 'Unicode?' "") (lift_to NameOrAddr (parseName c (eject c)))))))

  (define (parseName /*Unicode::*/ref /*string::*/ str)
    (if (string_holds_ion_identifier str)
      (inject_into Unicode str)
      (wrong "Malformed macro-ref: " (eject ref))))

  (define (parseNameOrAddr /*Unicode::*/ref /*string::*/ str)
    (if (string_holds_decimal_int str)
      (let [(i (with_ion_from_string str read))]
        (lift_to NameOrAddr (inject_into I i)))
      (if (string_holds_ion_identifier str)
        (lift_to NameOrAddr (inject_into Unicode str))
        (wrong "Malformed macro-ref: " (eject ref)))))

)
